Looking at this, I found the rule is **c = f(a)+g(b) mod 31** and **d = f(b)+g(a) mod 31** (i.e. the second output equals the first output of the swapped input). I reconstructed f and g from the data, which nailed dozens of transitions exactly.

A few queries use inputs (13, 21) or an isolated cluster (10,15,23,25) that never connect to the observed data, so those are estimates.

